<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's bank issues money supply statistics.</title>
<headline>Morocco's bank issues money supply statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) released on Monday its latest statistics on money supply during the month of February (billions of Moroccan dirhams at end period):</p>
<p>    1997	     M1	   M2	    M3</p>
<p>    Feb	     47.026     97.628     56.264</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Feb	     43.441     92.295     50.453</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>    Jan	     47.267     96.857     55.728</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Jan	     43.474     91.570     50.312</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Dec	     46.581     97.237     54.962</p>
<p>1995</p>
<p>    Dec	     43.261     92.703     50.552</p>
<p>The bank defined the agregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Banks cash holdings.</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Money + Deposit accounts.</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Quasi-money.</p>
<p>($1= 9.4 dirhams)</p>
</text>
